ironment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:60d668ee55a3c09c7830ba3ac7e7be9b1c8b6a7fbe7edb7930d47be91cb8f7f2","file":"preprints/Geometric-Programs-for-Solenoidal-Forcing-September-27-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":75,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"37ea205318d2e978047bd1c46848aa2048c16b40ed0c4f1a16294750a911e8cb","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/Geometric-Programs-for-Solenoidal-Forcing-September-27-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:60d668ee55a3c09c7830ba3ac7e7be9b1c8b6a7fbe7edb7930d47be91cb8f7f2","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Geometric-Programs-for-Solenoidal-Forcing-September-27-2026/build/introduction.tex#L75"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{sv:sheet-theorem}\nLet $P_i,Q_i\\subset[2,3]^2$, $1\\le i\\le N$, be closed rectangles\nwith rational vertices and positive side lengths.  Suppose the sources are pairwise\npositively separated and the targets are pairwise positively separated.\nLet $F_i:P_i\\to Q_i$ be the center-to-center affine map with any\npositive rational diagonal linear part, with $F_i(P_i)=Q_i$.  For each computable $\\nu>0$\nthere is an effective smooth mean-zero solenoidal force on\n$\\mathbb T_{10}^3$, one-periodic from time zero, whose unique solution\nin the classical class has pressure zero and period map\n\\[\n (y,2)\\longmapsto(F_i(y),2)\\qquad(y\\in P_i).\n\\]\nIts velocity is zero near integer times and has zero self-advection;\nall mixed derivatives of force and velocity are bounded.  No condition\nis imposed on source--target intersections.  For $N=0$ use zero."}
